## Implementation Summary

Implemented `BowlingGame` in `bowling.py` using a **roll-list + frame-indexed scorer**: every `roll(pins)` appends to `self.rolls`; `score()` iterates exactly 10 frames with a roll index, applying strike (`10 + next two`), spare (`10 + next one`), and open-frame rules. The 10th-frame fill balls are consumed naturally by the lookahead, so no special-casing is needed.

